**Point 9 – Step2 test metrics:**
- A new helper, `crt.step2_test_additions`, runs right after the original `export_test`, which is unchanged.
- It reads the exported `test_probabilities.npz` and uses the same `crt.evaluation` calculation as the cRT heads. It adds exactly two fields to `test_metrics.json`: `top5_accuracy` and `diagnostic_train_and_test_positive_classes`.
- It refuses to overwrite any existing field, so `loss_terms`, `selected_epoch`, `selection` and the fixed85 metrics stay as they are. It also writes the 85-row `test_class_counts.csv`.
- It runs only after the best checkpoint has been chosen, so it plays no part in selection.
- The trainer diff against the original (`crt_kpaths/review/step2_train_vs_original.diff`) now shows only this 4-line addition after `export_test`.

**Point 10 – docs:** `kpaths.py`, `README.md` and the summary now say that the official pipeline already merges parallel relations into composite relations before building the DiGraph (`merge_duplicate_relations`), and `get-subgraph.py` splits them back afterwards (`expand_relations`). Our relation tuples are described as an adaptation of that pipeline to DRKG's existing relation IDs, not a correction of it.

